\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
You may exit at any time by typing Ctrl-C or your operating system's end of file character (typically Ctrl-D or Ctrl-Z.) Typing Ctrl-C while code is executing will start a traceback and return to the REPL,
 if one was running.
 If your system has readline,
 you'll have familiar editing keys and a command history.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Common stack manipulation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
It's very common to manipulate the stack in several ways.
 The most common are DUP and DROP;
 DUP will duplicate the first level of the stack,
 and DROP will remove the most recent item from it.
 You can also switch the two most recent items around with SWAP:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
::
 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Hello!
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 #2 DUP
\end_layout

