 #1 'Counter >TYPE
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Registering a new type will make its type number available as Types.Counter and its name available in Types.n,
 just as all other objects.
 The prototype object is stored in Types.Proto.Counter,
 with the default value.
 To make a new object of a user type,
 it is generally sufficient to make a copy of the prototype object.
 By default,
 a user type will appear as a tag:
