\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph*
except
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When catching an error,
 the default 
\family typewriter
EXCEPT
\family default
 will first check to see if 
\family typewriter
except
\family default
 exists.
 If it does,
 it will be removed and evaluated.
 This leaves the main 
\family typewriter
EXCEPT
\family default
 routine in place to catch errors if the user-supplied 
\family typewriter
except
\family default
 fails.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph*
I*
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A directory of all the interpreter's Internal objects,
 documented in the final reference section of this document.
 On startup,
 this directory is quoted so it isn't readily accessible;
 internals are inherently unsafe and can readily cause crashes.
 To make it directly usable:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
I* 'I* STO
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph*
ISDED?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The interpreter's error state.
 This is only meaningful in concert with 
\family typewriter
DEDCONT?
\family default
.
 If an untrapped error has occurred,
 the error state is true:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
#1
\family default
 ⇒ error
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
#0
\family default
 ⇒ no error
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph*
TRACE?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
An integer number of running code blocks to leave on the call stack in case of an error.
 If unset,
 an error trace will back all the way out of the interpreter.
 In an interactive session,
 any REPL will temporarily set 
\family typewriter
TRACE?

\family default
 to its own depth.
\end_layout

